Introduction

   The object of the game is to kill other players in a maze. You will find
   grenades, trip mines and many other stuff...


Main menu

   After starting the game the main menu will appear. In the lower half of
   the screen the players in the maze are displayed. Before you enter the
   maze, you can change your enter status (see below) and choose a team.


Let's go

   After entering the maze it is displayed on the left half of the screen.
   You can only see these parts of the maze, which you have already
   discovered. Your status and a list of the players in the maze are
   displayed in the right half of the screen.

   Smbols in the maze

      ^ v < >    You, with view direction up, down, left and right

      i ! { }    The other players looking up, down, left and right

      - + |      Walls

      \ / #      Deflecting/dispersion walls

      ; g        Small and large mine

      :          Bullet

      o O        Grenade and satchel charge

      @          Bomb

      s $        Small and big slime

   Status display

      Ammo   - Ammo left
      Gun    - Status of your gun
      Damage - Actual/maximum damage
      Kills  - How many players you've killed

      Player - Players in the maze

   Display of Players

      The names of the players are displayed in the format
      <SCORE><STATUS><NAME><TEAM>.

      <SCORE>  - Player's score
      <STATUS> - Status (see below)
      <NAME>   - Name of the player
      <TEAM>   - Team (0-9 or nothing)

   Message display

      On the last line of the screen messages from other players and status
      messages are displayed.


Player's status

   A player can be in one of the following states:

   normal
      The player is visible to scanners from other players

   cloaked
      The player is invisible to scanners from other players

   scanning
      The player is using a scanner to view other players movements

   flying
      The player is flying over walls

   death :-)


Keyboard controls

   Movement

      <Cursor keys>     Move the player in the corresponding direction
      <w> <y> <a> <s>   Look up, down, left and right.

   Weapons

      <f>    Fire a bullet                (  1 Ammo)
      <g>    Throw grenade                (  2 Ammo)
      <1>    Throw satchel                ( 25 Ammo)

      <2>    Throw Bomb                   ( 49 Ammo)
      <3>    Throw big bomb               ( 81 Ammo)
      <4>    Throw even bigger bomb       (121 Ammo)
      <5>    Throw even more big bomb     (169 Ammo)
      <6>    Throw even more bigger bomb  (225 Ammo)
      <7>    Throw very big bomb          (289 Ammo)
      <8>    Throw very, very big bomb    (361 Ammo)
      <9>    Throw biggest bomb           (441 Ammo)

      <v>    Throw small slime            ( 15 Ammo)
      <b>    Throw big slime              ( 30 Ammo)
      <n>    Throw bigger slime           ( 45 Ammo)
      <m>    Throw biggest slime          ( 60 Ammo)

   Misc.

      <c>    Activate cloaking            (  1 Ammo)
      <x>    Activate scanner             (  1 Ammo)
      <q>    Quit

      <CTRL><L>    Redraw screen


Useful hints

    o You can only fire in the direction you are facing.

    o You can only fire three shots in a row, then the gun must cool off.

    o Shots move 5 times faster than you do.

    o To stab someone, you face that player and move at them.

    o Stabbing does 2 points worth of damage and shooting does 5 points.

    o Slime does 5 points of damage each time it hits.

    o You start with 15 charges and get 5 more every time a player enters
      or re-enters.

    o Grenade explosions cover a 3 by 3 area, each larger bomb cover a
      correspondingly larger area (ranging from 5 by 5 to 21 by 21).
      All explosions are centered around the square the shot hits and
      do the most damage in the center.

    o Slime affects all squares it oozes over. The number of squares is equal
      to the number of charges used.

    o One small mine and one large mine is placed in the maze for every new
      player.

    o A mine has a 2% probability of tripping when you walk forward on to it;
      50% when going sideways; 95% when backing up. Tripping a mine costs you
      5 points or 10 points respectively. Defusing a mine is worth 1 charge
      or 9 charges respectively.

    o You cannot see behind you.

    o Cloaking consumes 1 ammo charge per 20 of your moves.

    o Scanning consumes 1 ammo charge per (20 x the number of players)
      of other player moves.

    o Turning on cloaking turns off scanning / turning on scanning turns off
      cloaking.

    o When you kill someone, you get 2 more damage capacity points and 2
      damage points get taken away.

    o A shot destroys normal (i.e. non-diagonal, non-door) walls.

    o Diagonal walls deflect shots and change orientation.

    o Doors disperse shots in random directions (up, down, left, right).

    o Diagonal walls and doors cannot be destroyed by direct shots but may
      be destroyed by an adjacent grenade explosion.

    o Slime goes around walls, not through them.

    o Walls regenerate, reappearing in the order they were destroyed. One
      percent of the regenerated walls will be diagonal walls or doors.
      When a wall is generated directly beneath a player, he is thrown in
      a random direction for a random period of time.  When he lands, he
      sustains damage (up to 20 percent of the amount of damage already
      sustained); the less damage he had, the more nimble he is and therefore
      less likely to hurt himself on landing.

    o There is a volcano close to the center of the maze which goes off close
      to every 30 deaths.

    o Every 30 deaths or so, a '?' will appear. It is a wandering bomb which
      will explode when it hits someone, or when it is slimed.

    o If no one moves, everything stands still.

    o Your score is the decayed average of the ratio of number of kills to
      number of times you entered the game and is only kept for the duration
      of a single session of ahunt.


